WEBVTT

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.690
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.980
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.540
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.790
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.390
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:40.700
aoku hatenai sora no katasumi de
Newborn in a corner of the endless blue sky...

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:43.980
umareta yume ga
The dream is there,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:47.110
ima chiisakutemo
and even though it may now be small...

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.980
koori tsuku you na
No matter how strong they may blow...

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.960
tsuyoi kaze de sae
...or how icy they may be...

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.730
sono mune ni kagayaku
...those winds can never erase...

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:04.160
yume o keshitari, sou yo
...the dream that shines. Oh, no!

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.670
keshitari nante dekinai
The dream that shines inside your heart!

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.900
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:15.100
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.700
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.940
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.320
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.640
<i>Rear turrets! Do something</i>
<i>to suppress that lead Musai!</i>

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:44.880
<i>Ship number three's</i>
<i>been taken out!</i>

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.580
<i>Concentrate main guns</i>
<i>forward! Stop that thing!</i>

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.650
<i>It's too fast!</i>
<i>The predictor's useless!</i>

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:57.830
<i>Enemy mobile armor has broken</i>
<i>through defense line 3!</i>

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.800
<i>Speed: Mach 11 and decelerating!</i>

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.930
<i>9 seconds from</i>
<i>Jaburo firing range!</i>

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.510
Jaburo!

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.570
End simulation!

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.050
So, you're saying
they're planning to use...

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.450
...this new weapon to attack
Federation headquarters.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.620
Yes. According to the intelligence
we've managed to gather.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.120
Then we should begin.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:57.820
Yes, sir.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.460
Seek and destroy
the enemy base!

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:03.460
Synchronize watches!

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:06.660
Begin the operation!

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.180
A gun emplacement designed to dive
right down through the atmosphere.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:25.020
I think Revil's Antarctic Treaty
may have backfired on us.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:31.390
Captain, are you sure you made the
right decision about the 08th Team?

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.390
You mean that ensign?

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:38.300
His knowing an enemy pilot may
be an opportunity worth taking.

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:40.300
That's the reason you're!

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.670
Don't worry. I have an
insurance policy on this one.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.040
Two, in fact.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:48.700
Sanders, are you listening?

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:50.510
Yes, sir.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.710
After we make the drop
to point Alpha...

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.510
...we'll proceed to point Beta while
we search for the enemy base.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.820
We'll then rendezvous with the
recovery Medea and return to base.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:04.830
This operation is specifically
to find the enemy base.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:08.020
Getting intelligence
back is paramount.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.100
We have to do all we
can to avoid combat.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.900
So, you mean...

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:14.950
...even if that girl comes out at
us, we don't have to fight her!

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.740
"That girl"?

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:24.130
With the commander? Really?!
Oh, what the hell is this?!

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.740
All I had in that field hospital...

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:30.750
...were nurses who looked
like THIS, and you!

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.720
That's no fair! You rat!

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.920
He's full of himself.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.800
We should have some fun
of our own, right, Karen?

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.260
Eledore?

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:43.560
What?

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.100
Shut up!

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:51.270
What's wrong, Karen?
Why so cold?

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.970
I've never done
an air drop before...

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.840
...so I don't have time
to be bothered by you!

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.890
Get away.
You're annoying me...

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:01.680
Commander!

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.590
The truth is, I...

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:08.390
Five minutes to drop point!

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.280
All right, let's get
ready to move out.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:11.390
Roger!

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.460
Oh, well. Let's go.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:15.590
Sanders, you were about
to say something?

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.800
No, sir...

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.270
I see.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:26.770
So, is "that girl"
really pretty?

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.680
I dunno.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.650
Hey! Spy Guy!

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.810
Be careful.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:37.610
The commander isn't a spy!
He isn't crafty enough!

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.650
Okay, people, cut the chatter!

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:44.000
We're at the last point.
Better get into your coffins.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:46.890
Sanders, let's go.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:55.670
<i>Seal, confirmed.</i>

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:01.000
Night vision, activated.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.710
All I have to do is do
it like in the simulation.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:07.950
A Zeon girl pilot?!
God, talk about your romantics!

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.520
<i>A doomed love.</i>

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.480
Commander...
You can't be a spy.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.970
What the hell?! Commander!

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.880
<i>I've run into a Gaw!</i>
<i>Now engaging!</i>

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:37.710
Karen! Are you all right?!

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.310
Hurry up and drop us!

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:40.510
<i>Hang on a second!</i>

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.180
<i>If I send you out now,</i>
<i>we'll be in danger, too!</i>

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:44.620
Hurry!

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:51.980
Karen!
Don't stay still! Move!

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:54.460
Karen!

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:57.290
Darling, I'll be with you soon...

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:06.380
Machine, directly above us!

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.410
Get some flares up!

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:27.860
Dammit...

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:29.730
<i>Stop your shooting at once!</i>

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.770
<i>If you don't,</i>
<i>I'll shoot you down!</i>

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:40.900
<i>You're just going to shoot</i>
<i>yourselves down with me?</i>

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:53.650
Number two engine is on fire.

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:55.820
Put it out!

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:57.850
All gun turrets, cease fire!

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:01.390
<i>We're out of</i>
<i>their firing range!</i>

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.000
Do we fire, sir?

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:12.540
Forget him.
Our repairs come first.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:15.900
Why didn't he?

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:25.190
Aren't the rest of
our people here yet?!

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.310
That Gaw only had one
engine working, you know.

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:30.290
I've sighted what
looks like a Gaw!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.290
It's off the planned course!

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:34.290
Any Feddie planes near them?!

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.860
None! But it's trailing smoke.

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:39.770
Get some more people
on our defense line!

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:43.530
Please, let the engine be
the only trouble they had...

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.510
130...

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:57.550
120...

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:58.450
110...

00:08:58.560 --> 00:08:59.390
Fire!

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:08.130
Confirm landing!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.000
It's pretty...

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:21.700
<i>Karen! You okay?</i>

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:26.910
<i>Great location for inspiring</i>
<i>words of love, dontcha' think?</i>

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.680
You get a nice moment,
and then!

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:34.710
The opposite shore?
Where is it?

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:39.760
From the water?!

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:43.700
Karen!

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:07.420
No WAY you're
killing Karen!

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:10.690
<i>Michel, distract him</i>
<i>with the hovertruck!</i>

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:12.820
I can't use the
Vulcan if I'm alone!

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:14.860
<i>Would you rather let</i>
<i>my Karen die out here?!</i>

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:15.920
Oh, man...

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:18.390
Please! Hurry!

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:34.780
God dammit!

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:41.180
Karen! You hurt?!

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:43.590
Answer me!

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:46.120
Eledore?

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:50.220
Can you still use this?
Michel's in big trouble.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:52.840
But my monitor and
my scopes are out.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.240
No time for that!
I'll give you directions!

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:57.600
I'll be your targeter!
Get your beam rifle up!

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:02.310
A little to the right and up!

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:06.350
Too far! Down a little!

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:08.320
Stop!

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:13.150
He sees us!
Hurry up and fire!

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:17.520
Correct right, six degrees!
Here he comes!

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.830
<i>Fire! Fire!</i>

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:30.540
Eledore? Eledore!

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.520
ELEDORE!

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.690
Are you hurt?

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:53.920
Eledore!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.160
I think I pissed my
pants a little.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:58.430
You okay?

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.760
Thanks to you. You saved me.

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:05.670
Well, if you die, my whole
life plan gets thrown off.

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:22.160
We lost most of our cargo
as well as 14 personnel.

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:24.180
I'm sorry about this, sir.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:28.490
Forget it. It was my mistake to force
a crippled Gaw onto this mission.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.730
Forgive me.

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:32.770
Thank you, sir.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:36.600
You've done well.
Okay, let's get out of here.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:39.500
There's no way this smoke isn't
going to attract attention.

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.640
Even the Feddies aren't THAT dumb.

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:46.340
Sir!

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:50.580
Please lend me a few of these.

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:53.350
Those junk heaps?

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.580
You're not trying to
commit suicide, are you?

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:59.150
I want to buy some time for
our main force to pull out.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:02.160
And I owe that Feddie suit
with the face another look.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:07.870
As long as you promise to
come back from this alive.

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:09.900
I promise.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.200
I volunteer, sir!

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:14.470
Me, too.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:17.050
I can't promise you any
support or supplies!

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:19.270
We know that, sir.

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:21.250
Take care of
the soldiers, sir.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:22.790
Get 'em back into space, okay?

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:25.380
Men...

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:29.360
All right!
Magella Attack force, move out!

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:30.860
Sir!

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:34.790
Don't be mad.
C'mon, give me a break!

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:37.560
I've got the beam rifle
camera connected up!

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:40.790
I've got video on my scope!

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:44.710
I'll treat you when my
song's royalties come in!

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.780
Everyone, listen up!
We're changing the plan.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:53.980
Karen and the hovertruck will
head for the rendezvous point.

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:56.080
Sanders and I will
carry out the mission.

00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:59.220
We'll be in trouble
if we get in a fight.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.260
If you do, you do.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:02.620
Just run away
as fast as you can.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.960
You call that a plan?

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:07.700
Aye, sir. I will use my
state of the art mobile suit...

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:10.360
...to run away
as fast as I can!

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:24.850
I'm sorry about asking you
to help out down here.

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:27.910
It's all right. I know a bit
about medicines, after all.

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:29.950
I appreciate it.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.080
I'll help you.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:34.590
I'm fine.
Please, get some rest.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.460
I'll help you...

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:53.070
Y- You've been
giving them THIS?!

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.040
Yes.

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:57.640
And you call
yourself a <i>doctor?!</i>

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:01.910
To finish the Apsalus,
we have no choice.

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.450
My brother's orders, right?

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.620
No, it was my decision.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:10.580
As a doctor, my conscience
bothers me about it.

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:13.290
But we're also professional
soldiers who are...

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:17.530
...fighting a war for the
independence of the colonies!

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:21.800
With the Apsalus, we'll be able
to hit the enemy's headquarters.

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:25.600
And for that, as a soldier...

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:27.640
...I believe there are
things which must be done!

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:29.710
<i>I have to stop him.</i>

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.970
<i>He's even ignoring</i>
<i>the cancellation order!</i>

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:37.450
Looks like you managed to divert
those Rick Dom generators for yourself.

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:42.980
Of course. Cut phases 7, 8, and 9.
Hurry up on the construction!

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:46.690
Admiral Yuri is
requesting support.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:51.460
Support? And risk revealing
the location of this base?

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:54.090
But we can't stand by and
let our people get killed.

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:58.500
Let him deal with this himself.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.700
Sir, you should consider the
feelings of these soldiers...

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:03.540
...who have had such a hard
road to follow from Odessa.

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:05.650
Irrelevant.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.540
Nothing is more important
than the Apsalus's completion.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:13.490
Damn you, Ginias!
You'd abandon your own forces?!

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:20.290
I'm getting them back
into space, no matter what!

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:23.060
I'm counting on you,
Magella Attack team...

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:33.740
Commander...

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:35.000
Enemies?!

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.640
Something like that.

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:42.720
<i>I've been ordered to</i>
<i>keep an eye on you, sir.</i>

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:46.720
Because all I ever
do is break regs...

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.550
<i>Don't worry about it, Sanders.</i>

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.560
I figured Kojima would
do something like this.

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:59.500
Actually... It was
Captain Ryer's orders.

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:05.000
That guy...

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:10.910
Some of the men from the
inquiry must still not trust me.

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:12.640
Mines are now active!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.820
The Federation
doesn't trust me.

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:20.080
<i>Battle wreckage two klicks ahead!</i>
<i>Multiple metallic objects detected!</i>

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:22.120
<i>Perfect place for a trap...</i>

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:24.220
<i>Let's double back</i>
<i>into the forest.</i>

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:28.660
<i>Sanders! Pull back!</i>

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:31.130
<i>HEAT rounds, on the one</i>
<i>with the horns! FIRE!</i>

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:37.740
Switch to penetrator rounds!
Finish the horned one!

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:39.240
<i>FIRE!</i>

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:42.070
<i>Pulling out!</i>

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:43.740
<i>SANDERS!!!</i>

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:50.920
<i>Keep it up!</i>

00:17:50.990 --> 00:17:52.510
All units, fire HEAT rounds!

00:17:57.730 --> 00:17:59.190
He's got a lock! Pull back!

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:04.290
My optical sensors!

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:10.770
<i>Barry! Lunen! Formation A!</i>

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:14.440
<i>Once the smoke clears,</i>
<i>we settle things.</i>

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:17.110
<i>Let's try a little</i>
<i>psychological warfare...</i>

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:18.700
Federation mobile suit!

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.040
That voice!

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.610
<i>You're the captain of that Gaw!</i>

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.480
<i>Name's Bjorn Abust.</i>

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.680
I want to ask you something.

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:27.750
Why didn't you
open fire that time?

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:29.280
What?!

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:32.520
On behalf of my men, I want
to say they appreciated it.

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:34.650
But I can't agree with you!

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:38.600
We are Zeon! We don't need any
pity from some damned Feddie!

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:41.530
<i>I just wanted to</i>
<i>avoid needless deaths!</i>

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:43.200
<i>Will you still kill me</i>
<i>with that beam rifle?</i>

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.370
Thought so!

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:56.540
Our soldiers are suffering!
Please stop construction now!

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:06.630
And what then? Will you
stop this war yourself?

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:08.920
Hardly.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:13.060
But you've already received
the order to cease construction.

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.600
Forcing them take drugs to keep
working is meaningless now!

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:19.040
How moving...

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:21.200
However, we happen
to be fighting a war.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:24.450
The Apsalus WILL be completed.

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:27.850
I'm going to try to
get the order rescinded.

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:32.120
Hurry!

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:33.710
Sir, you should get in, too!

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.420
Don't be ridiculous!

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:37.290
I can't go in till
the others get back!

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:43.690
<i>Commander.</i>

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:44.890
Are you okay?

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:48.300
<i>My left leg's broken.</i>
<i>I can't help you.</i>

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:50.800
Are you bleeding?!
How bad is it?!

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:53.100
<i>No, the</i> mobile suit's <i>leg, sir.</i>

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:57.870
<i>I've forgotten the</i>
<i>most important thing.</i>

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:00.880
Are you going to shoot?!

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:01.740
YEAH!!!

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:08.610
All units,
fall back while firing!

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.420
Don't be in a hurry to die
now that we got this far!

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.450
<i>We've bought enough</i>
<i>time already!</i>

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.630
Right! If we're running,
leave it to me!

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:21.600
We've only been doing it all
the way from Odessa, after all!

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:26.900
Okay... Now let's finish this!

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:30.670
<i>I won't fight for</i>
<i>the Federation! However...</i>

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:33.680
I WILL fight for my friends!

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:36.290
And now you say that?

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:37.480
<i>I DON'T BELIEVE YOU!</i>

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:21.390
We have returned, sir!

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:24.890
I'm afraid we lost, though.

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:31.770
Glad you're back.
I really am.

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:35.040
Where's everyone else?

00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:37.710
They all made it inside,
thanks to you.

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:40.270
Now we can go
back into space.

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:43.080
I'll bet a fat-ass
like you prefers zero-G!

00:21:43.890 --> 00:21:45.790
Low blow, man!

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:47.350
Oh, lighten up.

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:50.880
What's up?

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:52.860
What's going on?

00:21:56.770 --> 00:21:58.760
<i>Rear Admiral Yuri Kellanay.</i>

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:00.100
Open up, Ginias!

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:03.470
Your private secretary
told me everything.

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:06.810
What have you
done to Cynthia?!

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:10.180
Commandant Giren still hasn't heard
about the cancellation order.

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:16.880
So, if you die in battle,
it will <i>never</i> reach headquarters.

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:19.950
Guys, run!
Get out of this tunnel!

00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:24.360
Admiral Kellanay was
honorably killed in action.

00:22:27.830 --> 00:22:29.260
Lunen! Barry!

00:22:31.930 --> 00:22:33.530
GINIAS!!!

00:22:36.570 --> 00:22:38.100
What?

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:56.420
osanaikoro kara
All that time that's passed me by.

00:22:56.490 --> 00:23:00.110
sou kyou made no so many days
From childhood till now, so many days.

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:04.250
furikaereba ironna
When I look back, I see so many things...

00:23:04.330 --> 00:23:08.020
koto ni meguriatta
...that happened to come into my life.

00:23:08.100 --> 00:23:11.190
naitari warattari
The times I cried, the times I laughed.

00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:15.200
kenka shitari yume mitari
The times I fought, the times I dreamed.

00:23:15.270 --> 00:23:19.330
chotto hard na shitsuren mo
The lost loves that were sort of hard.

00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:22.470
kagayaku my history
All shining in my history.

00:23:23.150 --> 00:23:25.610
ikutsumono
The ones who caused me pain...

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:30.480
deai to wakare kugurinukete
...I met and left along the way.

00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:36.350
ai suru anata ni sou yo
But I still ended up meeting you.

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:40.690
Love! meguriaeta
The one that I love.

00:23:42.130 --> 00:23:45.590
Ten years after juunen go no
Ten years after, A decade from now.

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:49.360
watashi wa doushiteru darou
I wonder what I will be doing then.

00:23:49.440 --> 00:23:56.500
donna fuu ni anata o sukideiru darou
I wonder how I will be still loving you.

00:23:57.280 --> 00:24:00.610
Ten years after, juunen go no
Ten years after, a decade from now.

00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:04.680
anata o mitsumete mitai
I still want to be looking at you.

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:08.420
Stay together sono toki
Stay together. When that day comes...

00:24:08.490 --> 00:24:15.110
kitto soba de hohoendeitai
...I want to be at your side with a smile.

00:24:18.910 --> 00:24:20.810
The Federal Forces finally
know the base's location...

00:24:20.880 --> 00:24:23.180
...and now a full-scale
battle has begun!

00:24:23.750 --> 00:24:26.920
Appearing before us
stands a blue mobile suit!

00:24:28.460 --> 00:24:30.290
If he can take on three
Gundams single-handedly...

00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:32.330
...he can only be
one thing... An ace!

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:36.690
One by one, he takes out
Federation soldiers, until finally!

00:24:37.170 --> 00:24:39.360
Am I going to die?!

00:24:40.900 --> 00:24:42.560
I've won!

00:24:43.340 --> 00:24:46.000
Next time,
"The Shuddering Mountain (Part 1)"
